  "title": "Gelati Monastery, Kutaisi",
  "summary": "Gelati Monastery near Kutaisi, Georgia, was begun in 1106 by King David IV the Builder as a royal burial place and a religious and educational centre. His son Demetre I completed the Church of the Nativity of the Virgin, consecrated in 1130, and 13th-century additions included St George, St Nicholas and a bell-tower.",
